/-
The index of the `ℓ ^ n`-th power subgroup of the unit group of a `p`-adic completion.

For `κ = K_𝔭` the `𝔭`-adic completion of a number field `K` (a local field of residue
characteristic `p`), a prime `ℓ ≠ p` and `n : ℕ`, the group `κˣ` of units of `κ` satisfies

  `[κˣ : (κˣ)^{ℓ ^ n}] = ℓ ^ n * gcd (ℓ ^ n) (#k - 1)`,

where `k` is the residue field of `κ` and `(κˣ)^{ℓ ^ n}` is the subgroup generated by the
`ℓ ^ n`-th powers.

The classical argument, formalised here:

* `κˣ ⊇ 𝒪_κˣ ⊇ U¹ = 1 + 𝔪` where `𝒪_κ` is the valuation ring and `𝔪` its maximal ideal;
* the valuation `v : κˣ → ℤ` is surjective (uniformiser) with kernel `𝒪_κˣ`, and `ℤ` is
  torsion free, so the general count
  `natCard_quot_powMonoidHom_eq_mul` splits off the factor `#(ℤ / ℓ^n ℤ) = ℓ ^ n`:
  `[κˣ : (κˣ)^{ℓ^n}] = ℓ ^ n * [𝒪_κˣ : (𝒪_κˣ)^{ℓ^n}]`;
* the residue map `𝒪_κˣ ↠ kˣ` is surjective with kernel `U¹`, and every element of `U¹` is an
  `ℓⁿ`-th power as soon as `ℓ ≠ p` (Hensel's lemma: `X^{ℓ^n} - u` has the simple root `1`
  modulo `𝔪` because `ℓ`, being different from the residue characteristic, is a unit);
  hence `(𝒪_κˣ)^{ℓ^n}` is the full preimage of `(kˣ)^{ℓ^n}` and
  `natCard_quot_powMonoidHom_eq_of_ker_le_pow` gives
  `[𝒪_κˣ : (𝒪_κˣ)^{ℓ^n}] = [kˣ : (kˣ)^{ℓ^n}]`;
* `kˣ` is finite cyclic of order `#k - 1`, so `[kˣ : (kˣ)^{ℓ^n}] = gcd (ℓ^n) (#k - 1)`
  (`card_quotient_powMonoidHom`).
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.Mine.UnitsAux
